        "original_id": "e2f62877-84c8-521f-b208-352944d9cc48",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franz Schreker, Luigi Cherubini, Ludwig van Beethoven\n- Works: Irrelohe\n- Roles: composer, conductor, teacher, administrator, librettist\n- Places: Monaco, Berlin, France\n\nFacts:\n- Luigi Cherubini was an Italian composer born on 8 or 14 September 1760 and died on 15 March 1842.\n- Luigi Cherubini spent most of his working life in France.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven regarded Luigi Cherubini as the greatest of his contemporaries.\n- Franz Schreker, originally named Schrecker, was born on 23 March 1878 in Monaco and died on 21 March 1934 in Berlin.\n- Franz Schreker was an Austrian composer, conductor, teacher, and administrator.\n- Irrelohe is an opera in three acts by Franz Schreker.\n- Franz Schreker wrote the libretto for Irrelohe.",
